  "session_id": "e5a8df68-3ae9-47fa-bfe7-34c28e8a18ec",
  "response": "I have implemented the asset loading logic for OpenClaw on Flipper Zero.\n\n1.  **Directory Structure**: Created `applications/external/openclaw/` to house the new code.\n2.  **Header File (`openclaw_assets.h`)**:\n    *   Defined `OpenClawSprite` and `OpenClawTilemap` structures.\n    *   Defined `OpenClawAssetManager` to hold storage reference and cache.\n    *   Declared functions for initialization, loading, and freeing assets.\n3.  **Implementation File (`openclaw_assets.c`)**:\n    *   Implemented `openclaw_assets_init` to open the `Storage` record.\n    *   Implemented `openclaw_load_sprite` and `openclaw_load_tilemap`:\n        *   Uses `storage_file_read` for efficient reading.\n        *   Reads directly into allocated memory to avoid double buffering.\n        *   Includes strict memory usage checks (32KB limit for sprites, 16KB for tilemaps) to prevent heap exhaustion on the Flipper Zero.\n    *   Implemented `openclaw_get_tile`:\n        *   Features a simple LRU (Least Recently Used) cache (`OPENCLAW_TILE_CACHE_SIZE = 16`).\n        *   Automatically manages cache eviction when full.\n        *   Loads tiles from `{tileset_path}/tile_{id}.bin` if not in cache.\n\nThe implementation relies on the standard Flipper Zero `furi` and `storage` libraries.\n\n**Files Created:**\n*   `applications/external/openclaw/openclaw_assets.h`\n*   `applications/external/openclaw/openclaw_assets.c`",
